Migrate Natron's remaining regular expressions to QtCore's Qt6 API.

Use QRegularExpression and explicit match objects, including highlighter
members and the optional matched-length completion branch. Whole-string
matches use anchoredPattern; backup suffixes use strict end-of-string
anchoring. Keep Unicode character classes and dot-all behavior where the
old patterns depend on them. Remove obsolete QRegExp and QDesktopWidget
includes.

Qt's standard wildcard conversion is not the old QRegExp dialect: it
restricts path separators, changes [!...] semantics, and does not implement
WildcardUnix escapes. Keep that dialect's focused pattern conversion in the
existing QtCompat namespace, with direct QRegularExpression callers (no
Core5Compat or QRegExp emulation). Searches remain unanchored; exact matches
are anchored. No Qt6.6 API or new Qt minimum is required.

The dialect translator is adapted from Qt's wc2rx:
https://github.com/qt/qt5compat/blob/6.6/src/core5/text/qregexp.cpp
